[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531628 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "901a723b-e6e5-572f-9b48-3f4f2a4dea43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "901a723b-e6e5-572f-9b48-3f4f2a4dea43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531175} :answer-field/id #uuid "3487b8fc-2024-52a0-8191-9d6c368ac790" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531427}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9290c4e-ece3-5a58-aecc-bb62b4894116" :question/math-academy-id "q-353582" :question/problem "![](images/83/83813bff1ff86036e2773d9476150de619688daec9cae2623a555a43290cace3.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{9}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}3\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531644 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ce61a52-02f8-52e3-833d-f0a747be827a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530920} {:answer/id #uuid "25efba17-6780-5d23-af19-6462827fe365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530950} {:answer/id #uuid "44549959-713e-5a87-987f-4262b4d5d3c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{\\sqrt{2}}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531009} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7da443-446d-582f-b934-dcaf57f4a7d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531287} {:answer/id #uuid "d25fbccb-dafe-5557-83e3-f260cee1b53a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25efba17-6780-5d23-af19-6462827fe365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530950} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a4caf7b-52fc-5e88-b891-82cc9a3a2cf7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "da080066-6980-5e46-a310-b96dc7f7120c" :question/math-academy-id "q-9540" :question/problem "![](images/c1/c1bf9d989f1fbaeda90325b924f2c9285cd4e37e1948ba63256258b0a84c7e44.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r={2}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={2}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }={2}^{\\theta }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({2}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{({2}^{\\theta }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{2}^{2\\theta }+{2}^{2\\theta }{ln}^{2}⁡2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(1+{ln}^{2}⁡2){2}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{2}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot {2}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot ({2}^{\\pi /2}-{2}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{\\pi /2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65e5c3f0-5773-5bbd-a23a-3a43d1fc086e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531761} {:answer/id #uuid "6b202fc5-7a82-5091-9da5-936069a8528b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{727}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531763} {:answer/id #uuid "9e2a14ab-0cce-5725-9c80-5f9d2f8d0921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "182" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531782} {:answer/id #uuid "bf400e9b-bb0b-5054-8ef9-7e5f7d9ae05b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "197" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531789} {:answer/id #uuid "f958d464-4ab0-5f12-8833-fb278b8eb146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{713}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f958d464-4ab0-5f12-8833-fb278b8eb146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{713}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531799} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c8c9430-d63b-5c40-bd47-a82c98a21776" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531746}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "01c658f5-4f30-5b39-9d41-0213df71f8bb" :question/problem "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $x=3.$ Given that the point $P(3,-4,6)$ lies on $C,$ and that $f_y = \\dfrac{5x}y - 5x^2y+2\\cos(\\pi y)$, find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=3.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P(3,-4,6)$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(3,-4).$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(3,-4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(3,-4) & =\\frac{5(3)}{(-4)}-5(3)^2(-4)+2\\cos(\\pi (-4)) \\\\  & =(- \\frac{15}{4})+(180)+(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{713}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05407676-cebb-5bc7-a937-477ac92325ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531734} {:answer/id #uuid "3399c19f-c144-565d-9a3f-74b3ab3c7fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{76}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531743} {:answer/id #uuid "6a768a59-5859-56ec-9a89-66c3e6901e41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531762} {:answer/id #uuid "87745150-95ec-582e-a5b6-e67dcf6fbdd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531774} {:answer/id #uuid "acd44b37-981b-5c47-acae-e2ba4562ebfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{68}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acd44b37-981b-5c47-acae-e2ba4562ebfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{68}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531784} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf0d0aa1-5612-5996-9db0-c13d0ba63c6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e5df7a0-85e1-5575-b4c1-bffca0c06fc3" :question/problem "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $x=2.$ Given that the point $P(2,-3,-8)$ lies on $C,$ and that $f_y = \\dfrac{2x}y - 2x^2y$, find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P(2,-3,-8)$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(2,-3).$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(2,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(2,-3) & =\\frac{2(2)}{(-3)}-2(2)^2(-3) \\\\  & =(- \\frac{4}{3})+(24) \\\\  & =\\frac{68}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531747 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16db819d-a31e-5205-8b7c-21af8af3e4c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{435}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531736} {:answer/id #uuid "3b56c38d-50f0-552e-ba37-defe41618c0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{429}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531745} {:answer/id #uuid "7f4ad521-1d5d-55b3-990a-6b4b3393ac6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "111" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531772} {:answer/id #uuid "a90c8bfd-a572-53b9-8c28-788ffabd340e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531783} {:answer/id #uuid "df2aad39-04a6-5fd1-9510-323e4332857b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16db819d-a31e-5205-8b7c-21af8af3e4c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{435}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531736} :answer-field/id #uuid "03f390c2-4771-5faa-ac0b-de2b80cc6c4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531733}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "43957037-7bd8-5b6e-bc6b-591297b827c3" :question/problem "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $x=3.$ Given that the point $P(3,-4,-6)$ lies on $C,$ and that $f_y = \\dfrac{3x}y - 3x^2y+3\\cos(\\pi y)$, find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=3.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P(3,-4,-6)$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(3,-4).$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(3,-4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(3,-4) & =\\frac{3(3)}{(-4)}-3(3)^2(-4)+3\\cos(\\pi (-4)) \\\\  & =(- \\frac{9}{4})+(108)+(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{435}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531767 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21fa2e46-9c3c-5506-8d21-503d32f1d649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531737} {:answer/id #uuid "22c0715a-7e0d-589f-ac97-e5653973417f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{170}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531738} {:answer/id #uuid "59e45521-5d59-508e-9ae3-52b0dfe26328" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531757} {:answer/id #uuid "c221dfd4-a68c-5273-9b59-b270d4ded14d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{190}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531790} {:answer/id #uuid "efd9ca39-e668-543d-8b5e-87683e083f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22c0715a-7e0d-589f-ac97-e5653973417f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{170}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531738} :answer-field/id #uuid "b