,-4) & =\\frac{3(3)}{(-4)}-3(3)^2(-4) \\\\  & =(- \\frac{9}{4})+(108) \\\\  & =\\frac{423}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531792 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2edbb6a3-36cf-5cc8-aaa0-ad4a7c8bbb91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531742} {:answer/id #uuid "461f7ce5-3c3c-53dc-a478-aa6deadab8c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{136}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531751} {:answer/id #uuid "4d73f21f-f03f-57d6-a4cc-500c581a4505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531752} {:answer/id #uuid "4eace776-fc53-5f37-a017-ed54121a6c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531753} {:answer/id #uuid "5c876e86-f759-5792-a2d0-6234c2caabe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{152}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c876e86-f759-5792-a2d0-6234c2caabe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{152}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531759} :answer-field/id #uuid "88e8a213-a421-58c8-943e-3fe579ce2651" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c56af156-4a29-5a55-8ac3-c69f2feb8c74" :question/problem "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $x=-2.$ Given that the point $P(-2,-3,-3)$ lies on $C,$ and that $f_y = \\dfrac{4x}y - 4x^2y$, find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solut